success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Kill the hidden session at once and power off (or reboot)

Usage: nails emergency [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -c, --config <PATH>
          Path to the configuration file (overrides binary-relative discovery)

      --countdown <SECS>
          Wait this many seconds before acting, printing a Ctrl+C abort hint.

          Omitted (the default) acts immediately. The wait is never affected by `--quiet` or `--json`, so output flags never change the timing.

      --poweroff
          Power off, also on the decoy side, where the emergency otherwise only cleans up. In the hidden session it powers off without the flag too. RAM decays: leave the machine off for a few minutes. Mutually exclusive with `--reboot`

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostics on stderr: -v for debug, -vv for trace

  -q, --quiet
          Print only errors and the final result

      --reboot
          Reboot fully (firmware and bootloader) instead of powering off.

          A warm reboot does not clear RAM. Prefer the power-off when RAM residue matters. Mutually exclusive with `--poweroff`.

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use colour

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal, TERM is not `dumb` and NO_COLOR is unset or empty
          - always: Always colour, even when piped
          - never:  Never colour

          [default: auto]

      --ascii
          Use ASCII markers instead of Unicode symbols and box drawing

      --json
          Print machine-readable JSON on stdout

      --no-log-file
          Do not write the log file on the hidden volume (diagnostics still go to stderr)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

WHAT HAPPENS:
  In the hidden session: every interactive shell is killed, the power-off is
  enqueued and every hidden program is killed at once. A hidden session never
  goes back to the decoy. With --reboot the machine reboots fully instead. On
  the decoy, emergency removes what an interrupted activation left in /run.

EXAMPLES:
  nails emergency                     Kill the hidden session and power off now
  nails emergency --countdown 5       Wait 5s (Ctrl+C to abort), then act
  nails emergency --reboot            Kill the hidden session and reboot fully

